        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is coherent, additive, and idiomatic for this codebase.\n\n- **Field/getter/setter in `Owner`** mirror the existing `bulkSignupWarning` member exactly (column annotation, accessor pair, advisory Javadoc), so a maintainer will recognize the pattern immediately.\n- **Threshold constant** `CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD` sits right next to and parallels `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD`, with a doc comment in the same style.\n- **Service logic is placed in the right unit.** The capacity warning belongs in the same `owner.isNew()` city-count block as the hard rejection, and folding the two into one block lets `countOwnersInCity(owner)` be computed once and reused for both the `>= MAX` rejection and the `>= WARNING` flag \u2014 this is a genuine improvement over calling it twice, not a duplication or a catch-all.\n- **Schema changes** are applied consistently across all four dialects in the same column position, matching the adjacent `bulk_signup_warning` column.\n- **OpenAPI** adds a `readOnly` boolean alongside the sibling advisory flags, consistent with how `possibleDuplicate` and the others are modeled.\n\nNothing is duplicated, no class or method is turning into a catch-all, and the logic lives where a maintainer would expect it."
